'\" t
.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
.TH CLEVO-CONTROL 7 "" "clevo-control @VERSION@" "Miscellaneous"
.SH NAME
clevo\-control \- keyboard backlight, Fn keys and performance profiles of Clevo laptops
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B clevo\-control
kernel module drives three functions of Clevo laptop firmware through standard
kernel interfaces, so that the desktop handles most of them by itself. The
tools around it are
.BR clevoctl (1),
.BR clevo\-control\-tray (1)
and a GNOME Shell extension.
.SS Keyboard backlight
An RGB keyboard is the LED
.IR /sys/class/leds/rgb:kbd_backlight ,
with attributes
.B brightness
(0\-255) and
.B multi_intensity
(three values in the order given by
.BR multi_index ).
Keyboards with three zones show the same color in all zones. The brightness is
remembered across reboots by
.BR systemd\-backlight@.service (8),
the color by
.B clevo\-control\-backlight.service
in
.IR /var/lib/clevo\-control/backlight\-color .
.SS Fn keys
With an RGB keyboard the module takes the backlight keys over from the
firmware. Key positions as found on the NH5x_NH7xHP (numeric keypad):
.TP
.B Fn + /
Next color: white, red, orange, yellow, green, cyan, blue, purple, pink.
Handled by the module.
.TP
.B Fn + *
Backlight on/off.
.TP
.BR "Fn + \-" ", " "Fn + +"
Brightness down/up.
.PP
On/off and brightness are reported as the keys
.BR KEY_KBDILLUMTOGGLE ,
.B KEY_KBDILLUMDOWN
and
.B KEY_KBDILLUMUP
and acted on by the desktop through
.BR upowerd (8).
Touchpad and airplane-mode events reported by the firmware are forwarded as
.B KEY_F21
and
.BR KEY_RFKILL .
Other Fn keys (volume, screen brightness, webcam) keep being handled by the
firmware or the regular keyboard driver.
.PP
On keyboards without RGB backlight the module leaves all keys to the firmware.
.SS Performance profiles
The firmware profiles are exposed as the kernel platform profile
.I /sys/firmware/acpi/platform_profile
(handler
.BR clevo ):
.TS
l l l.
platform profile	firmware profile	desktop power mode
_
quiet	quiet	Quiet (GNOME extension)
low\-power	power saving	Power Saver
balanced	entertainment	Balanced
performance	performance	Performance
.TE
.PP
.BR power\-profiles\-daemon (8)
switches the platform profile together with the desktop power mode. It reads
the available profiles when it starts.
.PP
The firmware cannot be asked which profile is active, nor whether it
implements the command. The module therefore offers the profiles only on
boards where their effect has been measured (or with
.BR force_profiles ),
sets
.B balanced
when it binds, reports the last profile it set, and sets it again after
suspend.
.SS Quiet in the GNOME power menu
The desktop's three power modes cannot select the
.B quiet
profile. The GNOME Shell extension
.B Clevo Control
.RI ( clevo\-control@pavelnikanovich.github.io )
adds a fourth entry,
.BR Quiet ,
to the Power Mode menu of the quick settings. While quiet is active
.BR power\-profiles\-daemon (8)
reports Power Saver, which is also what the Power panel of GNOME Settings
shows. If the menu cannot be extended, or the daemon is not running, the
extension shows a separate
.B Quiet Mode
toggle instead. Enable the extension once per user after logging in again:
.PP
.EX
gnome\-extensions enable clevo\-control@pavelnikanovich.github.io
.EE
.SS Permissions
A device rule gives the
.B plugdev
group write access to the color and brightness of the LED and to the platform
profile of the
.B clevo
handler.
.SH MODULE PARAMETERS
Set with
.B options clevo\-control
.IR name = value
in a file under
.IR /etc/modprobe.d/ .
.TP
.BR force_rgb =\fIY|N\fR
Treat the keyboard as 1-zone RGB when the firmware reports no RGB keyboard
(default N).
.TP
.BR force_profiles =\fIY|N\fR
Offer the performance profiles on a board they were not verified on
(default N).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/clevo\-control/backlight\-color
Remembered backlight color.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/70\-clevo\-control.rules
Permissions; starts the backlight service.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/clevo\-control\-backlight.service
Restores the color when the backlight appears, saves it when stopped.
.SH NOTES
The module needs Linux 6.14 or later. It conflicts with
.BR tuxedo\-drivers ,
which drives the same firmware interface.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR clevoctl (1),
.BR clevo\-control\-tray (1),
.BR powerprofilesctl (1),
.BR modinfo (8)
